    "authors": "Dionysia Katelouzou",
    "abstract": "Institutional investors have become some of the most influential actors in modern capitalism. They decide where vast pools of pension and other savings are invested, exercise shareholder rights across thousands of companies, and increasingly shape corporate responses to issues ranging from executive pay to climate change. Yet only a few decades ago, institutional shareholders were routinely criticised as passive or ‘absentee owners’.",
