    "title": "Precatory Proposals: A Broad Shareholder Right Under Delaware Law",
    "authors": "Salvatore Saltarelli",
    "abstract": "Do shareholders of Delaware corporations have any right to have their precatory proposals voted on at their general meeting? Or does the decision to call a vote belong entirely to the board? For more than eight decades, the federal proxy rules have required companies subject to those rules to include qualifying shareholder proposals in their proxy materials, enabling dispersed investors to communicate preferences, signal concerns, and influence corporate policy at relatively low cost.",
