    "title": "Power Tussle: Hedge Fund Activists and Short Sellers",
    "authors": "Tao Li",
    "abstract": "We study interactions between activist hedge funds and large short sellers using European data on activist campaigns and mandatory disclosures of large short positions. Large short sellers are associated with a 21% higher likelihood of activist targeting, higher campaign success, and profitability. Using the EU’s 2012 harmonization of short-position disclosure rules as an exogenous shock, we find causal evidence that the regulatory change affected activist targeting. Our evidence is consistent with an information channel: only hedge fund short sellers predict targeting, and the effects are amplified by information aggregation and disclosure novelty. Evidence on bargaining and cost channels is weaker.",
